 "title": "G5LE-E/-G: single-pole sugar-cube PCB power relay, 16 A 250 VAC (-E) or 10 A 35 VDC (-G)",
 "source": {
  "revision": "no revision printed; PDF dated 2006-11-12",
  "pages": 5
 },
 "summary": "A small cube-shaped through-hole power relay with one pole, in SPDT or SPST-NO form, on a common five-pin footprint. The -E high-capacity type switches 16 A at 250 VAC resistive with a 400 mW coil (or 360 mW for -E-36); the -G type has a 0.8 mm contact gap and switches 10 A at 35 VDC with a 700 mW coil. The coil has class F (155 °C) insulation, the case is flux-protected, the tracking index is CTI>250, and coil to contacts withstands a 4,500 V impulse. It is RoHS compliant. The G5LE-1-E DC5 is the SPDT -E type with a 5 VDC coil of 62.5 Ω drawing 80.0 mA.",
