  "notes": [
   "The code reads G5LE, then 1 (one pole), then nothing for SPDT or A for SPST-NO, then the classification: E for the high-capacity type or G for the 0.8 mm contact gap type. A -36 suffix (E only) gives the approx. 360 mW coil; without it an E coil is approx. 400 mW and a G coil approx. 700 mW. The coil voltage follows the number.",
   "Insulation is class F (155°C) on every model. Rated coil voltages are 5, 12 and 24 VDC for E types and 9, 12, 20 and 24 VDC for G types.",
   "An SP suffix orders anti-static tube packing; without it the relays come in polystyrene trays."
  ]
